WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.350
In February 2020, the
US economy hit a peak.

2
00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:06.890
By April, it had hit bottom.

3
00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:09.560
That recession lasted just 2 months:

4
00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:12.480
the shortest US recession on record.

5
00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:17.020
The one that began in December
2007 lasted 18 months.

6
00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:20.160
So why does an economy
grow in bursts and slumps

7
00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.330
instead of at a steady pace?

8
00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:25.250
In this mission, you'll
map the business cycle:

9
00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:28.900
expansion, peak, recession and trough.

10
00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:31.340
Then you'll use a graph lab to open a gap

11
00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:34.150
between actual and potential output.

12
00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:38.720
Your mission: find out why
real GDP expands and contracts

13
00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:40.360
instead of climbing steadily.
